      "problem": "Find the measure of an angle that's supplementary to an angle of $(7x -63)^\\circ.$",
      "worked_solution": "Two angles are supplementary if their measures add up to $180^\\circ.$ \n\nSo, the measure of an angle that's supplementary to an angle of $(7x -63)^\\circ$ must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}-(7x-63)^{∘} & =(180-7x+63)^{∘} \\\\  & =(180+63-7x)^{∘} \\\\  & =(243-7x)^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
